9:["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","h1",null,{"id":"changelog","children":"Changelog"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Beta channel: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"0.1.0-beta.x"}],". Breaking changes ship in\nany beta release — each one is listed at the top of its\nentry below, with no migration scripts until 1.0. No\nsilent breaks: removed verbs/flags fail loud naming the\nreplacement."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["Engine v2. Seven verbs, file-backed memory, MCP-only\ncomposition. For the version-matched agent contract at\nany time: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"agent-webmcp skill show"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"id":"unreleased-beta","children":"Unreleased (beta)"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Breaking:"}]," the config system is removed. No files,\nno schema, no served ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/config.json"}],", no ",["$","code",null,{"children":"config"}]," key in\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"doctor"}],". The two launch options stay plain flags:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"--consequential allow|ask|deny"}]," (default ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ask"}],", bad\nvalues exit 2) and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--registry DIR"}],". ",["$","code",null,{"children":"doctor"}]," reports\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"policy: {value, source: flag|default}"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Breaking:"}]," the config file system is dead. Deleted:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"AGENT_WEBMCP_CONFIG"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"AGENT_WEBMCP_CONFIG_CONTENT"}],",\nproject/global files, walk-up, substitution. Policy is\none flag per invocation: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"--consequential allow|ask|deny"}]," (default ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ask"}],"), garbage fails loud at\nstartup. Enforcement must live server-side — the gated\nagent supplies ",["$","code",null,{"children":"confirm"}]," itself and project files can't\nconstrain a harness-controlled cwd. Gate logic\nuntouched; ",["$","code",null,{"children":"doctor"}]," reports flag or default."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Breaking:"}]," config shrinks to one key and the endpoint\nleaves it entirely. Deleted: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"browser.cdp"}]," (the driver\nfeeds the endpoint per ",["$","code",null,{"children":"open"}]," call via ",["$","code",null,{"children":"cdp"}],"; discovery\ncovers daemon → 9222/9229, else fail loud) and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"index.enabled"}]," (consult always, degrade on miss — the\nflag bought nothing). Remaining: ",["$","code",null,{"children":"permissions.conse- quential"}]," (",["$","code",null,{"children":"ask"}],"|",["$","code",null,{"children":"allow"}],"|",["$","code",null,{"children":"deny"}],", default ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ask"}],"), the\nsafety catch on mutating page tools, opencode-shaped\n(same three effects; headless, so ",["$","code",null,{"children":"ask"}]," means the call\nmust carry ",["$","code",null,{"children":"confirm: true"}],"). Old keys are ignored, not\nerrors — no migration needed. Malformed files now warn"]}],"\n",["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["skip (opencode ",["$","code",null,{"children":"parseInfo"}],") instead of failing loud\non explicit paths; new ",["$","code",null,{"children":"{file:path}"}]," substitution for\nsecrets."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Breaking:"}]," registry env deleted, global-main confirmed.\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"AGENT_WEBMCP_REGISTRY"}]," is gone — ",["$","code",null,{"children":"mcp serve --registry DIR"}],"\npins the root, otherwise project ",["$","code",null,{"children":".agent-webmcp/registry/"}],"\noverlays the user-global main store (reads merge, project\nwins). The double-append walk-up bug is fixed (production\nwalk-up never hit; everything silently fell back to\nglobal). Malformed config files now warn + continue like\nopencode instead of failing loud on explicit paths; new\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"{file:path}"}]," substitution for secrets (relative to the\nconfig file's dir)."]}],"\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15"],null,"$L16"]}]
